{"kind":"request","text":"NF5 has one concrete lifecycle API gap before drain source. Custody.#write(id,record,true) commits phase sent before the deliver call (custody.ts original535-555). The store sees that mark and the identity lock, but cannot tell held-after-mark/before-POST from a genuinely in-flight network operation. Holding the DB for every marked/locked identity could admit work never dispatched and let a never-settling network promise block versionchange forever.\n\nPlease rule on these boundaries:\n1. May an identity already delivering its same envelope create only bounded outcome/segment/readback transactions on the old connection after close, and if so how must Custody tell the store that actual deliver began (the dispatch flag is too early)? No new signing, admission, resubmit, preparation or capability step would receive this permission.\n2. For versionchange, should the DB close immediately after currently CREATED IDB transactions drain? Then a later network result cannot start bookkeeping and Custody must report its existing unkept storage outcome while retaining the exact sent record; no cleared slot/acceptance is claimed. This avoids an unbounded schema block. Or must we hold an explicitly bounded grace for the already delivered same-envelope result? Please name the termination rule; I will not invent a timeout.\n3. Custody.#write performs a second store.read after store.write. I can verify put/get bytes within the same readwrite IDB transaction and await complete, but the generic read still follows. Should an already admitted write/readback operation finish before connection close, or should a post-close read reject even if the write committed (retaining safe but possibly conservative unkept classification)?\n\nProposed witnesses use gates: hold after sent mark before deliver (zero POST after retirement); hold actual POST forever then request schema upgrade (no indefinite blocked upgrade); release actual POST after retirement (exact sent original retained and the ruled result/unkept status); retire during a created result transaction (real commit/abort truth). Root requested this follow-up. Independent bounded-row/format source repair continues; no project execution.","body":{"conditions":"Define the permitted result-bookkeeping boundary after store retirement and versionchange without treating sent as proof of actual network dispatch or indefinitely blocking a schema change.","no_git_artifact":"true","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}